I come out of the office during the lunch break.
The road outside is very busy.
Many people are walking on the pavement.
A tourist comes towards me.
He looks a little confused.
He has a map in his hand.
He politely asks me, "Excuse me, Madam."
I stop and smile.
He asks, "Where is the big post office?"
I know this area very well now.
I confidently tell him the way.
I say, "The post office is further ahead on this very road."
"Do you see that big intersection?"
He nods and says, "Yes."
I say, "The post office is right next to the intersection."
"It is a very large and red building."
The tourist looks happy.
He says, "Thank you very much, Madam."
I smile and reply, "No problem."
He walks ahead in the direction of the post office.
